From 56ba1bc419c395a8ba128bb4a98414ebc42e1389 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Erben <a.erben@qvest-digital.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 08:35:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mxl-gst-testsrc): overlay on I420, convert to v210 once
 at the end
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The producer pipeline generated v210 at the source and ran the pango
text/clock overlays directly on it. Pango renders RGBA and blends
per-frame; on v210 (10-bit packed 4:2:2) at 1080p that is several times
more expensive than on 8-bit planar I420, and it pushed the pipeline
below the grain rate.

Once the producer can't make frames at the grain rate, the bounded
drop=true appsink sheds ~half of them and the commit loop backfills the
skipped indices with INVALID grains (~50% backfill observed). Every
consumer — local read and cross-node RDMA mirror alike — then plays an
irregular, gap-filled sequence: motion stutters and appears to jump.

Generate and overlay in I420, then a single videoconvert produces the
v210 the flow requires. The pipeline sustains the full grain rate, the
appsink stops dropping, and backfill falls to ~0 (measured 50%/s -> ~0).
Also drops the dead videoscale (no scaling was configured).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/mxl-gst/testsrc.cpp | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/mxl-gst/testsrc.cpp b/tools/mxl-gst/testsrc.cpp
index 6d0d5f63..44730031 100644
--- a/tools/mxl-gst/testsrc.cpp
+++ b/tools/mxl-gst/testsrc.cpp
@@ -342,12 +342,21 @@ namespace
             MXL_INFO("Creating video pipeline with config: {}", _config.display());
 
             auto pipelineDesc = fmt::format(
+                // Generate + overlay in 8-bit planar I420, convert to v210 ONCE
+                // at the end. The pango overlays (text/clock) render RGBA and
+                // blend per-frame; doing that on v210 (10-bit packed 4:2:2) at
+                // 1080p is several times more expensive and pushed the producer
+                // below the grain rate — the appsink then dropped ~half the
+                // frames and libmxl backfilled the gaps, so every consumer
+                // (local and cross-node) saw jerky, stale motion. Overlaying on
+                // I420 lets the pipeline sustain the full frame rate; a single
+                // videoconvert produces the v210 the flow requires.
                 "videotestsrc name=videotestsrc is-live=true do-timestamp=true pattern={} ! "
-                "video/x-raw,format=v210,width={},height={},framerate={}/{} ! "
+                "video/x-raw,format=I420,width={},height={},framerate={}/{} ! "
                 "textoverlay text=\"{}\" font-desc=\"Sans, 36\" ! "
                 "clockoverlay ! "
                 "videoconvert ! "
-                "videoscale ! "
+                "video/x-raw,format=v210 ! "
                 // leaky=downstream: drop the oldest buffer when full instead
                 // of back-pressuring the live source. Without this a slow
                 // consumer makes the source throttle to the consumer rate and
